{
  "spec": "priest-discipline",
  "state": "written",
  "notes": "Discipline priest healer rotation, written against the fork's fake raid: the healer is raid player 0, the four fake party members are players 1 to 4 and the tank is player 5. Reference build: 33 points in Discipline and 18 in Holy (engine talent string 005203031305101531-0350500302: Twin Disciplines 5, Silent Resolve 2, Improved Power Word: Shield 3, Mental Agility 3, Inner Focus, Meditation 3, Mental Strength 5, Soul Warding, Penance, Renewed Hope 5, Divine Aegis 3, Power Infusion; Improved Renew 3, Holy Specialization 5, Divine Fury 5, Inspiration 3, Improved Healing 2). Penance is cast on its cooldown at whoever is hurt, the tank is shielded when he is hurt and Weakened Soul is off, and the filler is Heal. Power Infusion is only used when the player names a target for it; the major-cooldown pass casts it. Renew is left out on purpose: against the fork's test profile it returned less health per mana than Penance and Heal. Mana: the list opens with the autocast line, which is how the Major Mana Potion, the Demonic Rune and Inner Focus are used (each fires whenever it is ready and the bar has room for it; Inner Focus goes on whichever priest spell is cast next). Mana pacing: the filler, Prayer of Healing and Power Word: Shield fire at their normal thresholds only while the mana bar is at least 90% of the share of the fight left (currentManaPercent against remainingTimePercent); behind that pace the filler waits for a tank under 50% and a member under 35% and the shield waits. Penance and the emergency Flash Heals are never paced. Ranks follow one rule, stated in design/reviews/2026-10-08-healer-mana-audit.md: starting from the top ranks, a lower rank (never one learned below level 20) is taken for a spell when it raises the ranker's guarded score by more than two percent, the biggest gain first, the tank's casts and the party members' casts counted apart, and compared on the raid gear the ranker published for the list being tried. The engine states the client's own numbers for every rank with no downrank penalty, so a lower rank is a statement about this profile, not a measurement of the game. The site runs this list as written at band 60 and lifts every ranked spell to the highest rank learned below it. Here that is Prayer of Healing at rank 1 and Power Word: Shield at rank 4; every other spell keeps its top rank. The comparison is repeated on the gear each new list makes the ranker choose until no spell moves. The review lists what each rank returned.",
